# AI-BOS Marketing OS Binding

When working in the Marketing OS lane, treat delivery context as **`PRJ-GRO-MKOS-001`**.

## Mandatory

1. Read `AI-BOS/project-registry/registry.json` entry `PRJ-GRO-MKOS-001` before material marketing work.
2. Load `RU-AI-BOS-MKOS-001` + `HB-GRO-MKOS-001` + division handbook for assigned agent.
3. Persist outcomes under `founder-os-memory/projects/<slug>/marketing/` per `ST-GRO-MKT-MEMORY-001`.
4. End with Bangla handoff per `RU-AI-BOS-HANDOFF-001`.

## Routing

| Need | Agent |
|------|-------|
| Marketing entry / multi-channel | `@marketing-cmo` (`AG-GRO-CMO-001`) |
| Offer / funnel (early) | `@founder-marketing` → escalate to CMO when channels multiply |
| Business context | `@founder-os` |
| Site implementation | `@frontend-architect` / `@frontend-content-strategist` |
| Sales handoff | `@founder-sales` |
| Vault / registry | `@system-builder` |

## Human gates (never automate)

Ad spend, ad account creation, OAuth, publish to social, email send — stop with Bangla click-by-click instructions.

## Never

- Write product code in marketing agents — delegate to `AG-DLV-*`
- Fabricate analytics or performance data
- Skip claims review (`ST-GRO-CLAIMS-001`) on external copy

Knowledge-layer mirror: `RU-AI-BOS-MKOS-001`.
